[0.008,"o","\u001b[H[![\u001b[38;5;12m\u001b[48;5;1mBuild\u001b[m](\u001b[38;5;13mhttps://github.com/guitarrapc/scenetake/actions/workflows/build.yaml/badge.svg\u001b[m)](\u001b[38;5;13mhttps://github.com/guitarrapc/scenetake/actions/workflows/build.yaml\u001b[m)\u001b[4;1H[![\u001b[38;5;12m\u001b[48;5;1mLicense: MIT\u001b[m](\u001b[38;5;13mhttps://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg\u001b[m)](\u001b[38;5;13mLICENSE\u001b[m)\r\n[![\u001b[38;5;12m\u001b[48;5;1mNuGet\u001b[m](\u001b[38;5;13mhttps://img.shields.io/nuget/v/scenetake.svg?label=scenetake%20nuget\u001b[m)](\u001b[38;5;13mhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/scenetake\u001b[m)\r\n[![\u001b[38;5;12m\u001b[48;5;1mnpm\u001b[m](\u001b[38;5;13mhttps://img.shields.io/npm/v/scenetake.svg?label=scenetake%20npm\u001b[m)](\u001b[38;5;13mhttps://www.npmjs.com/package/scenetake\u001b[m)\u001b[38;5;9m\u001b[10;1H# \u001b[38;5;13mscenetake\u001b[m\u001b[12;1HEnglish | [\u001b[38;5;12m\u001b[48;5;1m日本語\u001b[m](\u001b[38;5;13mREADME-ja.md\u001b[m)\r\nRecorded with scenetake.\u001b[15;1HRun a YAML \u001b[38;5;15m**scenario** \u001b[mand record a terminal scene take [\u001b[38;5;12m\u001b[48;5;1masciinema v3 \u001b[38;5;9m\u001b[49m`\u001b[m.cast\u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m](\u001b[38;5;13mhttps://docs.asciinema.org/manual/asciicast/v3/\u001b[m), animated \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m.svg\u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m. You do not need to install or launch \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[masciinema\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[mto record. Write a YAML scenario with steps, and this tool executes those steps and records the output as \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m.cast\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[m(and optionally \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m.svg\u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m)—ordinary steps get simulated typing; steps with \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[mpty: true\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[mcapture the terminal stream in real time.\u001b[22;1HSample scenario \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[msamples/basic.yaml\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[mgenerates "]
